</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="float: left; width: 48%; margin-right: 2%;">
        <img src="placeholder_image_3.png" alt="Installation of accessory for auxiliary power connection" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
        <div class="figure-caption">Fig.16: <span data-field="figure_caption_3">{{ figure_caption_3 }}</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="float: right; width: 48%;">
        <h3>Connecting load connection of MCB for accessories</h3>
        <p>RPP-X2-X3-INT-X4-X6-X7-X8</p>
        <ul>
            <li>To connect the <span data-field="pole_count_1">{{ pole_count_1 }}</span> MCB on the DIN rail use CU cables with a minimum diameter of <span data-field="min_diameter_1">{{ min_diameter_1 }}</span></li>
            <li>To connect the MCCB with the MCB on the DIN rail use cable lugs to connect the cable to the MCCB</li>
            <li>This "small" cable lug with a minimum cross section of <span data-field="small_lug_cs">{{ small_lug_cs }}</span> should be above the other "big" cable lugs with a cross section of <span data-field="big_lug_cs">{{ big_lug_cs }}</span> or <span data-field="big_lug_cs_2">{{ big_lug_cs_2 }}</span> as mentioned in Fig.15</li>
        </ul>
        <img src="placeholder_image_4.png" alt="Pin terminals example" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-top: 20px;">
        <div class="figure-caption">Fig.17: <span data-field="figure_caption_4">{{ figure_caption_4 }}</span></div>
        <ul>
            <li>Use insulated pin terminals as shown in Fig. 17 to connect the wires to the 4-pole MCB on the DIN rail</li>
            <li>This is needed to ensure IP20B</li>
        </ul>
        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
            <h4>Mounting of protection housing of MCCB</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>Assemble the electrical shock protection.</li>
                <li>Depending on the size of the cables it is necessary to break out the plastic cover as less as possible.</li>
                <li>Fix the protection housing - "High terminal cover" - using the tiny screw.</li>
                <li>For further information please refer to the assembly manual, provided with the "High terminal cover"</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
